                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1]What Makes This Game S.P.E.C.I.A.L.[/h1]\n[url=http://steamcommunity.com/id/KyleJames0408]Key to the Review[/url]\n[b]S[/b] • 1/10 | This game is just terrible as a whole, no strengths to speak of.\n[b]P[/b] • 3/10 | Sounds and feels decent but looks atrocious. Possibly untextured [spoiler]monster[/spoiler].\n[b]E[/b] • 1/10 | Could not endure more than 12 minutes, zero replayability.\n[b]C[/b] • 1/10 | I felt enraged that somebody would pay 100 dollars to publish this game on Steam\n[b]I[/b] • 3/10 | Poor story in [spoiler]notes[/spoiler] and a useless [spoiler]Katana[/spoiler]. Lame ways to die.\n[b]A[/b] • 1/10 | Takes less than ten minutes to complete the game.\n[b]L[/b] • 5/10 | Luck to skill ratio is fair. Find some things by luck, others by skill.\n\n[h1]Original Review[/h1]\nHello Fellow Office Workers,\nThis is by far the most pointless game I've ever played. Here are your options once you read all of the notes and understand the story. You can burn yourself to death by, count it, four different ways, you can kill yourself in a washing machine, you can kill yourself with a katana, you can kill yourself by trying to hit the monster with the katana, or you could get out of the elevator with the monster and die. So basically, you die five different ways throughout the game. If you decide that you think you can take the monster on with the katana, you might be there leveling your katana up forever since there's literally no point in doing it. The game is ridiculously weird and stupid. I do not recommend.",
